# GOAD-Cloud Architecture

## Overview

GOAD-Cloud is a serverless platform that runs automated security assessments against an Active Directory environment hosted on AWS. Users initiate scans via a web dashboard; results are delivered as PDF reports identifying attack paths and misconfigurations.

The system uses a stateless, event-driven architecture: each component does one job and communicates with others through AWS-managed services (S3, DynamoDB, SSM). No long-running servers process scan requests — scans execute on demand and shut down when idle.

